  "raw": " in his bid to disentangle America’s finances from years of debt accumulation and slow growth.\n\nAmericans’ belief that their retirement savings aren’t enough is undermining morale about investing in future generations, according to data released this spring by custodian Fidelity Investments [FISCWDQ]. Since 2009, people younger than 35 have pulled nearly $6 trillion out of their retirement accounts – almost twice as much money as they put into them all those years.\nAmericans‘ retirement confidence ranks last among the developed nations surveyed for the annual survey by Fidelity Northeast, in a list topped by Japan just above England, Italy...[Full Article...]\n\nAmericans think their retirement savings are for today rather than tomorrow? Sure, but what we found even more encouraging was who exactly Americans feel their retirement savings should belong to: Those old enough to remember India's pay me back revolution when Asia shock waves obliterated at least a third of its industrialized economy. And Americans' overall",
